+
+# Personal API tokens for the JSON API
+
+## Context
+
+Authors publish from scripts by replaying login cookies against the HTML
+pages, which breaks whenever a page changes. They need a JSON API with
+credentials they create and revoke themselves, and operations needs a
+ceiling on what any one script can send.
+
+## Decision
+
+- **Tokens are the framework's own.** `createApiToken()` issues
+  `<id>|<secret>`; the `api_tokens` table keeps the id and a SHA-256 of the
+  secret, through `DatabaseApiTokenStore`. The plain token exists only in
+  the 201 response that creates it.
+- **A token is accepted under `/api` and nowhere else.** The store is not
+  registered with `auth.useTokens()`, which would make a bearer header
+  answer for the session on every route: a leaked token could then change
+  its owner's password or mint more tokens. `/profile/tokens` takes a
+  signed-in session only.
+- **`/api` reads no cookies, so it is excluded from CSRF protection.** A
+  bad or missing token answers 401 there instead of a CSRF 403.
+- **The rate limit is 60 requests a minute per token**, keyed on the
+  verified token's id and applied after authentication, so failed
+  attempts spend nobody's allowance. It is a fixed window that opens with
+  a token's first request; `Retry-After` is what is left of it.
+- **Counters are held in process memory.**
+
+## Consequences
+
+- Revoking deletes the row, so it takes effect on the next request and
+  leaves the owner's other tokens alone.
+- A route added to `routes/api.ts` must authenticate by token: anything
+  there that trusted a session would have no CSRF protection.
+- Rate-limit counters reset on restart and are not shared between
+  processes. Running more than one needs a shared store
+  (`RedisRateLimitStore`), or each process grants its own 60.
+- Requests that fail authentication are not throttled by this limit.
+- `abilities` and `expiresAt` exist as columns because the store writes
+  them. Every token is issued with all abilities and no expiry; scopes and
+  expiry are not implemented.
+- `GET /api/posts` returns every post. Paging was out of scope and will
+  be needed as the table grows.
